/* AVIS.ARTIFACT
   FILE: avis.fvs
   NAME: AVIS_NAVIGATOR
   ROLE: Root navigation artifact for folder-drop-in compatibility

   PURPOSE:
       - Serves as the entry point for any AVIS-enabled folder
       - Provides navigation to all .defs, .artifact templates, and .art identity files
       - Establishes AVIS folder structure without requiring installation
       - Enables AVIS systems to auto-detect and auto-load artifacts
       - Acts as the FVS (File Visibility System) root

   WRAPS:
       avis_cmt_artifacts.def
       avis_cmt_artifacts.defs
       avis_c_artifacts.defs
       avis_h_artifacts.defs
       avis_cmt.artifacts

   MAPS:
       TEMPLATES: *.artifact
       ARTIFACTS: *.art
       DEFINITIONS: *.defs
       WRAPPERS: *_wrap.art

   SUBSYSTEM:
       FAMILY: AVIS
       LAYER: Navigation
       TIER: 0
       STATUS: Active

   IDENTITY:
       VERSION: 1.0
       AUTHOR: AVIS System
       CREATED: <Date>
       UPDATED: <Date>
       SIGNATURE: AVIS-FVS-NAV-ROOT

   DESCRIPTION:
       This file is the AVIS navigator. It is the first file loaded by any
       AVIS-aware system. It defines the folder structure, the template
       architecture, and the DEFS linkage. It enables drop-in compatibility
       by providing a single, stable entry point that requires no external
       configuration.

   NOTES:
       - This file must always be named avis.fvs
       - This file must always exist at the root of the AVIS folder
       - This file contains no code; it is identity and navigation only
       - This file is mandatory for AVIS folder portability

   REGISTRY:
       - Root of AVIS template registry
       - Root of AVIS DEFS registry
       - Root of AVIS artifact registry

   LAW:
       PREFIX: AVIS_
       NAMING: Navigator must be named avis.fvs
       STRUCTURE: Must contain WRAPS and MAPS blocks

   HISTORY:
       [v1.0] Initial navigator creation

   FUTURE:
       - Auto-discovery of new DEFS files
       - Auto-expansion of template categories
       - Integration with AVIS runtime loaders
*/
